  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "Triangles \\(ABC\\) and \\(ADC\\) are isosceles with \\(AB=BC\\) and \\(AD=DC.\\) Point \\(D\\) is inside \\(\\triangle ABC,\\) \\(\\angle ABC=40^\\circ,\\) and \\(\\angle ADC=140^\\circ.\\) What is the degree measure of \\(\\angle BAD?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(20\\)",
    "B": "\\(30\\)",
    "C": "\\(40\\)",
    "D": "\\(50\\)",
    "E": "\\(60\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Both isosceles triangles have base \\(AC\\), so each has equal angles at \\(A\\) and \\(C\\). Using the triangle angle sum gives\n\\[\n\\angle BAC=\\frac{180^\\circ-40^\\circ}{2}=70^\\circ\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n\\angle DAC=\\frac{180^\\circ-140^\\circ}{2}=20^\\circ.\n\\]\nBecause \\(D\\) is inside \\(\\triangle ABC\\), ray \\(AD\\) lies inside \\(\\angle BAC\\). Therefore\n\\[\n\\angle BAD=70^\\circ-20^\\circ=50^\\circ,\n\\]\nchoice D.",
